---
title: DndController API
description: Full API reference for DndController — reactive getters, event callbacks, methods, and types.
---

# DndController API

The `DndController` is the core engine that manages all drag-and-drop state and logic. You can create one explicitly or let `DndProvider` create one automatically.

## Constructor

```ts
import {
    DndController,
    PointerSensor,
    KeyboardSensor,
    centerPoint,
    overlap,
    restrictToVerticalAxis,
    defaultAnnouncements,
} from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

// Minimal — all options have sensible defaults
const controller = new DndController();

// Full config:
const controller = new DndController({
    behaviors: [                                // see /docs/behaviors
        autoScroll({ zoneRatio: 0.2, maxSpeed: 20, stopOnDrop: true }),
        scrollSync({ threshold: 0.5 }),
    ],
    animation: {
        preview: {
            showDelay: 150,                                       // ms before preview slot appears (default: 300)
            hideDelay: 400,                                       // ms before slot collapses (default: 200)
            show: { duration: 250, easing: 'ease-out' },          // CSS reveal transition (default: 200ms ease)
            hide: { duration: 200, easing: 'ease-in' },           // CSS collapse transition (default: 200ms ease)
        },
        siblingShift: { duration: 220, easing: 'ease' },          // sibling translate + cross-container spacer
        ghostResize: { duration: 180, easing: 'ease-out' },       // ghost auto-resize on cross-container moves
        drop: 200,                                                // ghost flight on successful drop (default: 250)
        return: 250,                                              // ghost return on cancelled drag (default: 300)
        slotCollapse: 200,                                        // source slot collapse on cross-container drop (default: 250)
        layout: 280,                                              // animateLayout default (default: 300)
    },
    debug: true,                             // position validation warnings in console
    sensors: [new PointerSensor(), new KeyboardSensor()], // see /docs/sensors
    collision: overlap('25%'),               // see /docs/collision
    modifiers: [restrictToVerticalAxis],      // see /docs/modifiers
    announcements: {                          // see /docs/accessibility
        ...defaultAnnouncements,
        onDragStart: ({ item }) => `Picked up ${item.id}.`,
    },
});

// Default values (what you get when omitting each option):
const controller = new DndController({
    behaviors: [autoScroll(), scrollSync()], // controller-level defaults; see /docs/behaviors
    animation: {
        preview: {
            showDelay: 300,
            hideDelay: 200,
            show: { duration: 200, easing: 'ease' },
            hide: { duration: 200, easing: 'ease' },
        },
        siblingShift: { duration: 200, easing: 'cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)' },
        ghostResize: { duration: 150, easing: 'ease' },
        drop: 250,
        return: 300,
        slotCollapse: 250,
        layout: 300,
    },
    debug: false,
    sensors: [new PointerSensor(), new KeyboardSensor()],
    collision: centerPoint,  // ghost center must be inside zone rect (default)
    modifiers: [],
    announcements: {
        onDragStart: ({ item }) => `Started dragging item ${item.id}.`,
        onDragOver: ({ item, current }) => `Item ${item.id} is over ${current.id} at position ${current.position}.`,
        onDrop: ({ item, target }) => `Dropped item ${item.id} into ${target.id} at position ${target.position}.`,
        onCancel: ({ item }) => `Dragging ${item.id} was cancelled.`,
    },
});
```

Pass it to the provider via the `controller` prop:

```svelte
<DndProvider {controller}>
    <!-- your DnD content -->
</DndProvider>
```

This gives you direct access to the controller's methods and reactive getters.

## Reactive Getters

All getters are Svelte 5 reactive (`$state` / `$derived` internally).

| Getter | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `dragging` | `boolean` | Whether a drag is currently in progress |
| `element` | `HTMLElement \| null` | The DOM element being dragged |
| `transform` | `{ x: number; y: number } \| null` | Current ghost position |
| `draggedItem` | `string \| null` | ID of the item being dragged |
| `draggedType` | `string \| null` | Type of the dragged item (from the `type` prop on `DndDraggable`) |
| `draggedItemData` | `Record<string, unknown> \| undefined` | Data attached to the dragged item |
| `ghostSize` | `{ width: number; height: number } \| null` | Size of the dragged element |
| `animatingReturn` | `boolean` | Whether the ghost is animating back to origin |
| `dropPreview` | `DropPreview \| null` | Current drop preview state |
| `dropPreviewSize` | `{ width, height } \| null` | Reactive size for matching the drop target's layout. Cross-axis is taken from the target's first non-dragged item (where layout shrinkage shows up — e.g. a scrollbar narrowing items); main-axis stays from the dragged item. Vertical sortable → target width / dragged height; horizontal sortable → dragged width / target height; grid sortable → both from target; target() containers → `null`. The built-in ghost and preview already use it. |
| `dropZones` | `DropZone[]` | All registered drop zones |
| `performingDrop` | `boolean` | Whether a drop animation is in progress |
| `dragSource` | `DragSource` | `'user'` during a real drag, `'programmatic'` during a simulation |

## Event Callbacks

All event methods return an unsubscribe function.

### onDragStart

```ts
const unsubscribe = controller.onDragStart(({ item, source }) => {
    console.log('Started dragging:', item.id, 'from', source.id, 'at position', source.position);
});

// Later: unsubscribe()
```

### onDragEnd

Fired when a drag ends — regardless of whether it was dropped or cancelled.

```ts
controller.onDragEnd(({ item, source, target, cancelled }) => {
    if (cancelled) {
        console.log(item.id, 'returned to', source.id);
    } else {
        console.log(item.id, 'moved to', target?.id);
    }
});
```

### onDropCancelled

Fired when a drag is cancelled — the ghost returns to origin and no drop occurred. Use this to distinguish a cancel from a successful drop.

```ts
controller.onDropCancelled(({ item, source }) => {
    console.log('Drag cancelled:', item.id, 'back to', source.id);
});
```

### onDrop

The main callback for handling item reordering or moving between containers.

```ts
controller.onDrop(({ item, source, target }) => {
    // item.id:          ID of the dragged item
    // item.data:        Record<string, unknown> | undefined — cast to your type as needed
    // source.id:        container the item came from
    // source.position:  original position in source container
    // target.id:        container where item was dropped
    // target.position:  insertion index in target container
});
```

> **`position` semantics** — `position` is an **insertion index**, not an index into your data array. `0` means before all items, `items.length` means after all items. For a `target`/`current` position, it's the slot between items where the dragged item would be inserted.

### onDragOver

Fired each time the drag-over target (container + position) changes. Useful for highlighting the active drop zone in custom UIs.

```ts
controller.onDragOver(({ item, current, previous }) => {
    console.log(item.id, 'moved to', current.id, 'position', current.position);
    if (previous) console.log('was over', previous.id);
});
```

### onZonesInvalidated

```ts
controller.onZonesInvalidated(() => {
    // fired after auto-scroll moves a container,
    // invalidating existing drop zone coordinates
});
```

Subscribe to recalculate zones if you manage them manually.

## Methods

### updateTransform

```ts
controller.updateTransform(transform: { x: number; y: number }): void
```

Updates the ghost element position during drag.

### updateMousePosition

```ts
controller.updateMousePosition(mouseX: number, mouseY: number): void
```

Updates the mouse position for drop zone detection and auto-scroll.

### performDrop

```ts
controller.performDrop(
    sourceId: string,
    sourceData: Record<string, unknown> | undefined,
    targetContainerId: string,
    position: number
): void
```

Performs a drop with animation to the target zone.

### endDrag

```ts
controller.endDrag(shouldAnimate?: boolean): void
```

Ends the drag. When `shouldAnimate` is `true` (default), the ghost animates back to its origin.

### setBehaviors

```ts
controller.setBehaviors(behaviors: Behavior[]): void
```

Replaces the controller-level default `behaviors` at runtime (see [Behaviors](/docs/behaviors)). Per-strategy `behaviors` set on a `sortable()` / `target()` instance are unaffected. Changes take effect on the next scroll tick / drop animation.

```ts
controller.setBehaviors([
    autoScroll({ maxSpeed: 60 }),
    scrollSync({ threshold: 0.5 })
]);
```

### setAnimation

```ts
controller.setAnimation(config?: AnimationConfig): void
```

Updates the controller's animation config at runtime. Accepts a partial — provided fields override, omitted fields keep their current value. Changes propagate reactively to every live `DndPreview`, `DndDraggable`, `DndDroppable`, and apply to the next drop / return / FLIP animation.

```ts
// tweak only the preview hide delay; everything else keeps its current value
controller.setAnimation({ preview: { hideDelay: 500 } });

// switch the sibling-shift to a different easing without changing duration
controller.setAnimation({ siblingShift: { easing: 'ease-out' } });
```

### setDebug

```ts
controller.setDebug(value: boolean): void
```

Toggles dev warnings (duplicate positions, etc.) at runtime.

### setSensors

```ts
controller.setSensors(sensors: SensorDescriptor[] | undefined): void
```

Replaces the active sensors at runtime. Pass `undefined` to fall back to the default `[PointerSensor, KeyboardSensor]` set.

### setAnnouncements

```ts
controller.setAnnouncements(announcements: Announcements | undefined): void
```

Replaces the screen-reader announcement strings at runtime. Pass `undefined` to restore the defaults.

### setModifiers

```ts
controller.setModifiers(modifiers: Modifier[]): void
```

Replaces the active transform modifier pipeline. Pass an empty array to disable all modifiers.

### toggleDebugZones

```ts
controller.toggleDebugZones(): void
```

Toggles visual overlay of all drop zones. Useful for development and debugging.

### destroy

```ts
controller.destroy(): void
```

Cleans up all internal state, listeners, and registries. Called automatically when `DndProvider` unmounts (if it created the controller).

## Programmatic Animations

For running animations without user interaction see the [Simulations](/docs/simulations) page.

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `animateItem(itemId, options)` | Fly one item to a destination through the ghost system. Pass `style: 'return'` for scroll-aware undo, `emitEvents: true` to fire `onDrop`/`onDropCancelled`. |
| `animateLayout(applyState, options?)` | Mutate state inside `applyState`; the library FLIPs every item whose rect changed. Pass `morph: true` to also transition class-driven properties. |

## Types

All types below are exported from `@horuse/svelte-dnd`.

```ts
interface DropZone {
    containerId: string;
    position: number;
    layout: DndLayout;
    itemId?: string;
    rect: { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number };
}

interface AutoScrollConfig {
    /** Fraction of container size that triggers auto-scroll. Default: 0.3 */
    zoneRatio?: number;
    /** Maximum scroll speed in px/frame at 60fps. Default: 30 */
    maxSpeed?: number;
    /** Stop auto-scroll immediately when drop is committed. Default: false. */
    stopOnDrop?: boolean;
}

interface ScrollSyncOptions {
    /**
     * Visibility ratio (0..1) below which the drop / return animation scrolls
     * the destination container in lockstep with the ghost flight. Default: 1
     * (any hidden pixel triggers scroll). Set 0 to disable.
     */
    threshold?: number;
}

// Built-in behavior factories — see /docs/behaviors
declare function autoScroll(opts?: AutoScrollConfig): Behavior;
declare function scrollSync(opts?: ScrollSyncOptions): Behavior;

type Transition = {
    /** Duration in milliseconds. */
    duration: number;
    /** Any valid CSS timing-function: 'ease', 'cubic-bezier(...)', 'linear', etc. */
    easing?: string;
}

interface AnimationConfig {
    preview?: {
        /** Debounce delay (ms) before revealing the preview slot. Default: 300 */
        showDelay?: number;
        /** Delay (ms) before collapsing the preview slot. Default: 200 */
        hideDelay?: number;
        /** CSS transition for the reveal (opacity / scale). Default: 200ms ease */
        show?: Transition;
        /** CSS transition for the collapse. Default: 200ms ease */
        hide?: Transition;
    };
    /**
     * Items repositioning to make room for the ghost — covers BOTH intra-container
     * sibling translate AND cross-container spacer growth. One field, both effects.
     * Default: 200ms cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)
     */
    siblingShift?: Transition;
    /**
     * Ghost auto-resize transition when crossing containers with different item
     * dimensions. Default: 150ms ease
     */
    ghostResize?: Transition;
    /** Ghost flight to a destination on successful drop (rAF, ms). Default: 250 */
    drop?: number;
    /** Ghost return flight on cancelled drop (rAF, ms). Default: 300 */
    return?: number;
    /** Source slot collapse on cross-container drop (rAF, ms). Default: 250 */
    slotCollapse?: number;
    /** Default duration for `animateLayout()` FLIP transitions (ms). Default: 300 */
    layout?: number;
}

interface DndControllerConfig {
    /** Drop-side plugins (auto-scroll, scroll-sync, future hooks). Default: `[autoScroll(), scrollSync()]`. See [Behaviors](/docs/behaviors). */
    behaviors?: Behavior[];
    animation?: AnimationConfig;
    /** Enable dev warnings (duplicate positions, etc.). Default: false */
    debug?: boolean;
    /** Active input sensors. Defaults to [PointerSensor, KeyboardSensor]. See [Sensors](/docs/sensors) */
    sensors?: SensorDescriptor[];
    /** Global collision algorithm. Per-container `collision` prop takes priority. See [Collision Detection](/docs/collision) */
    collision?: CollisionAlgorithm;
    /** Transform modifiers applied to ghost position on every move. See [Modifiers](/docs/modifiers) */
    modifiers?: Modifier[];
    /** Screen-reader announcement strings. See [Accessibility](/docs/accessibility) */
    announcements?: Announcements;
}

// Per-container strategies are now passed to `<DndDroppable strategy={...} />`
// rather than to the controller. See [Custom Strategies](/docs/custom-strategies).

// Rich event objects passed to all callbacks:
interface DndItemInfo {
    id: string;
    data: Record<string, unknown> | undefined;
    type: string | undefined;
    element: HTMLElement;
}
interface DndContainerInfo {
    id: string;
    data: Record<string, unknown> | undefined;
    layout: DndLayout;
    mode: DndMode;
    disabled: boolean;
    accepts: string | string[] | undefined;
    position: number;
}
interface DragStartEvent     { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo }
interface DragEndEvent       { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo; target: DndContainerInfo | null; cancelled: boolean }
interface DropEvent          { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo; target: DndContainerInfo }
interface DragOverEvent      { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo; current: DndContainerInfo; previous: DndContainerInfo | null }
interface DropCancelledEvent { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo }

type DragStartCallback    = (event: DragStartEvent) => void;
type DragEndCallback      = (event: DragEndEvent) => void;
type DropCancelledCallback = (event: DropCancelledEvent) => void;
type DropCallback         = (event: DropEvent) => void;
type DragOverCallback     = (event: DragOverEvent) => void;
type DndLayout = 'vertical' | 'horizontal' | 'grid';
type DndMode = 'sortable' | 'target' | (string & {}); // custom modes allowed
type DragSource = 'user' | 'programmatic';
```

For custom drop zone strategies see [Custom Strategies](/docs/custom-strategies).
